IO-59: print a space before each flow value in the summary tables

DefaultReportPlugin's flowFmt() copies the legacy "%9.2f" / "%9.3f", so
flows of 100,000.00 or more (10,000.000 in MGD or CMS) run into the
preceding value in the Node Inflow Summary, e.g. "150000.00150000.00".
Use " %8.2f" / " %8.3f": every value that fits prints exactly as before,
and a larger one is still separated by a space.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-59_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp b/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
index 0c601fa..af8a86b 100644
--- a/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
@@ -148,9 +148,11 @@ static const char* lt_str(int lt) {
 
 #define WRITE(f, s) std::fprintf(f, "\n  %s", s)
 
-// Flow format string (legacy: "%9.3f" for MGD/CMS, "%9.2f" otherwise)
+// Flow format string (legacy: " %8.3f" for MGD/CMS, " %8.2f" otherwise);
+// the leading space keeps a flow too large for its column from merging
+// with the preceding value
 static const char* flowFmt(int fu) {
-    return (fu == 2 || fu == 3) ? "%9.3f" : "%9.2f";
+    return (fu == 2 || fu == 3) ? " %8.3f" : " %8.2f";
 }
 
 // Project land-area units → internal ft². Subcatchment area is stored in
